blocks.en:
Figure 6: CN vs. AD classification: AUC improvement over baseline with 95% CI (5 × \times 5 repeated stratified cross-validation). Combining volume with all uncertainty metrics improved CN vs. AD classification by +0.06 AUC ( p < 0.001 p<0.001 ). Y-axis (top to bottom): Vol_ensemble_mean = baseline (TIV-normalized bilateral hippocampal volume);
Full_LR/Full_mean = all features (volumes + uncertainty metrics, L/R separate or averaged);
Vol+UQ variants = volume combined with uncertainty;
Vol_all_tools_mean = per-tool volumes;
Vol_LR_separate = left/right volumes;
Vol_raw_mean = unnormalized volume;
UQ variants = uncertainty only (variance, mutual information), aggregated by mean/sum/max over ROI or whole image.
All volume-based sets include age and sex as covariates.

